Every SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit runs the CLI, so its load time is paid per session and per prompt.

Measured:
- k188 (throwaway CLI.pm copy): loading past --version/--help lazily cuts warm --version of the packed binary by 100-120 ms (to 266-301 ms), cold by 70-100 ms; status/check unchanged. Deferring Encode as well adds only 15-25 ms.
- k181: `hook user-prompt-submit` with nothing due costs about what `require Skilletor::CLI` costs (~240 ms of ~240 ms; perl -e 1 is 9 ms). Most of it is Moo and namespace::clean pulled in through Skilletor::Error::JSON, plus Path::Tiny, Encode and JSON::MaybeXS. The hook itself adds State and Config (~45 ms) and never the engine.

Do: load in Skilletor::CLI only what --version, --help, a usage error and the hook fast path need; keep t/69 fast-path test (no engine) and add one for the modules a --version run loads. Measure before/after for perl -Ilib and the packed binary (perl/scripts/build-binary.sh) and put the numbers on the card.

